WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.151
This paper, A View From Somewhere,

00:00:02.231 --> 00:00:07.203
published at ICLR 2023 by researchers at Sony AI
and the University of Tokyo,

00:00:07.283 --> 00:00:10.484
rethinks how we represent human faces in datasets.

00:00:10.564 --> 00:00:15.274
Instead of relying on problematic demographic
labels like race or gender,

00:00:15.354 --> 00:00:21.179
the authors collect over six hundred thousand human
judgments of face similarity and learn

00:00:21.259 --> 00:00:25.050
a continuous embedding space aligned with human
perception.

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:28.856
The result is a face representation that is interpretable,

00:00:28.936 --> 00:00:33.449
that avoids invasive categorical labels, and that
captures the smooth,

00:00:33.529 --> 00:00:36.598
continuous nature of human phenotypic diversity,

00:00:36.678 --> 00:00:41.060
opening a new path for measuring dataset diversity
more responsibly.
